  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Test Name</div></th><th><div>Normal Range</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Antiphospholipid Antibodies, IgG</div></td><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>A positive result may indicate antiphospholipid syndrome or another autoimmune disorder, thrombosis or recurrent miscarriages. Further evaluation may be necessary.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Antiphospholipid Antibodies, IgM</div></td><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>A positive result may indicate antiphospholipid syndrome or another autoimmune disorder, thrombosis or recurrent miscarriages. Further evaluation may be necessary.</div></td></tr></tbody></table><p style=\"text-align: start\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: start\">It's important to note that a positive result for Antiphospholipid Antibodies test does not necessarily mean a person has a health condition. Additional testing and evaluation is necessary for an accurate diagnosis.<br></p>",
